IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ap-dates`
IMPORT `ap-duties`
IMPORT `ap-intestacy`
IMPORT `ap-seat`

-- Administration and Probate Act 1958 (Vic), Part IA -- worked cases for the claimant's intestacy questions (ap-seat.l4).
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts and the statutory legacy of
-- $500,000 are illustrative (the real figure for a year is in the Minister's Gazette notice, not deposited).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases: Part IA`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

GIVEN w IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A NUMBER, l IS A NUMBER, i IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A NUMBER, t IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A partner's entitlement`
`entitlement` w c l i b t MEANS
    `A partner's entitlement` WITH
        `the whole residuary estate` IS w
        `the personal chattels, by value` IS c
        `the statutory legacy` IS l
        `interest on the statutory legacy at the legacy interest rate` IS i
        `the share of the balance` IS b
        `the total, before interest` IS t

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What I must pay into the estate`
`payment of` a `by` day MEANS
    `What I must pay into the estate` WITH
        `the amount` IS a
        `the last day` IS day

§§ `s 70A, s 106 -- do the intestacy rules apply`

#ASSERT `Do the intestacy rules apply` (`d` 1 11 2017) `no will` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do the intestacy rules apply` (`d` 31 10 2017) `no will` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Do the intestacy rules apply` (`d` 1 1 2026) `a will that does not effectively dispose of the whole estate` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Do the intestacy rules apply` (`d` 1 1 2026) `a will that effectively disposes of the whole estate` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Do the intestacy rules apply` (`d` 31 10 2017) `a will that effectively disposes of the whole estate` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 70C -- surviving by 30 days`

-- Arguments: day of their death, I have died, day I died, today, otherwise to the Crown. Death on 1 March 2026: 31 March is
-- the 30th day after.
#ASSERT `Did I survive long enough to share` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 31 3 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS `I survived the intestate by at least 30 days, so I may share`
#ASSERT `Did I survive long enough to share` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 3 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS `I did not survive the intestate by 30 days, so I am taken to have predeceased`
#ASSERT `Did I survive long enough to share` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 30 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `30 days have not yet passed since the death`
#ASSERT `Did I survive long enough to share` (`d` 1 3 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 31 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS `I survived the intestate by at least 30 days, so I may share`
#ASSERT `Did I survive long enough to share` (`d` 1 3 2026) TRUE (`d` 2 3 2026) (`d` 1 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS `the 30-day rule does not apply, because the estate would otherwise pass to the Crown`
-- Across 29 February 2028: 1 February to 2 March is 30 days, to 1 March 29.
#ASSERT `Did I survive long enough to share` (`d` 1 2 2028) TRUE (`d` 2 3 2028) (`d` 1 6 2028) FALSE EQUALS `I survived the intestate by at least 30 days, so I may share`
#ASSERT `Did I survive long enough to share` (`d` 1 2 2028) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2028) (`d` 1 6 2028) FALSE EQUALS `I did not survive the intestate by 30 days, so I am taken to have predeceased`

§§ `Divisions 3, 5 and 6 -- who takes`

-- Arguments: partners, child lines, issue not of a partner, parents, sibling lines, remote sibling issue, grandparents,
-- aunt and uncle lines, estate worth, statutory legacy.
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 1 0 FALSE 2 3 FALSE 2 4 1000000 500000 EQUALS `the partner takes the whole (s 70J)`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 1 2 FALSE 2 3 FALSE 2 4 1000000 500000 EQUALS `the partner takes the whole (s 70K)`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 1 2 TRUE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 500000 500000 EQUALS `the partner takes the whole, as it is worth no more than the statutory legacy (s 70L(1)(a))`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 1 2 TRUE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 500001 500000 EQUALS `the partner takes the chattels, the statutory legacy with interest and half the balance; the children's lines take the other half (s 70L(1)(b), (2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 2 0 FALSE 2 0 FALSE 0 0 1000000 500000 EQUALS `the partners share the whole (s 70Z)`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 2 1 FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 1000000 500000 EQUALS `the partners share the whole (s 70ZA)`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 2 1 TRUE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 400000 500000 EQUALS `the partners share the whole, as it is worth no more than the statutory legacy (s 70ZB(1)(a), (b))`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 2 1 TRUE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 900000 500000 EQUALS `the partners share the chattels, the statutory legacy with interest and half the balance; the children's lines take the other half (s 70ZB(1)(c), (2), (3))`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 0 3 FALSE 2 3 FALSE 2 4 900000 500000 EQUALS `the children's lines take the whole (s 70ZG)`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 0 0 FALSE 1 2 FALSE 2 4 900000 500000 EQUALS `the parents take the whole (s 70ZH)`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 0 0 FALSE 0 2 FALSE 2 4 900000 500000 EQUALS `the siblings' lines take the whole (s 70ZI)`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 0 0 FALSE 0 0 TRUE 2 3 900000 500000 EQUALS `the Crown takes the whole, though a sibling's remoter issue survives (s 70ZL; finding 2)`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 0 0 FALSE 0 0 FALSE 2 3 900000 500000 EQUALS `the grandparents take the whole (s 70ZJ)`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 0 0 FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 3 900000 500000 EQUALS `the aunts' and uncles' lines take the whole (s 70ZK)`
#ASSERT `Who takes the estate` 0 0 FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 900000 500000 EQUALS `the Crown takes the whole (s 70ZL)`

§§ `ss 70J-70L, 70Z-70ZE -- what a partner takes`

-- Arguments: partners, child lines, issue not of a partner, estate worth, chattels worth, statutory legacy, agreement or order.
-- $1,000,000 with $50,000 chattels and a $500,000 legacy: the rest after chattels $950,000; legacy $500,000; balance $450,000,
-- half $225,000; total $775,000.
#ASSERT `What do I take as the partner` 1 2 TRUE 1000000 50000 500000 FALSE EQUALS JUST (`entitlement` FALSE 50000 500000 TRUE 225000 775000)
#ASSERT `What do I take as the partner` 1 0 FALSE 1000000 50000 500000 FALSE EQUALS JUST (`entitlement` TRUE 50000 0 FALSE 0 1000000)
#ASSERT `What do I take as the partner` 1 2 FALSE 1000000 50000 500000 FALSE EQUALS JUST (`entitlement` TRUE 50000 0 FALSE 0 1000000)
#ASSERT `What do I take as the partner` 1 2 TRUE 500000 50000 500000 FALSE EQUALS JUST (`entitlement` TRUE 50000 0 FALSE 0 500000)
-- Just over the legacy, with chattels: $520,000 less $50,000 chattels leaves $470,000, all of it legacy; no balance (fork F4).
#ASSERT `What do I take as the partner` 1 2 TRUE 520000 50000 500000 FALSE EQUALS JUST (`entitlement` FALSE 50000 470000 TRUE 0 520000)
-- Two partners in equal shares (s 70ZE): halves of the s 70ZB(1)(c) amounts.
#ASSERT `What do I take as the partner` 2 1 TRUE 1000000 50000 500000 FALSE EQUALS JUST (`entitlement` FALSE 25000 250000 TRUE 112500 387500)
#ASSERT `What do I take as the partner` 2 0 FALSE 900000 30000 500000 FALSE EQUALS JUST (`entitlement` TRUE 15000 0 FALSE 0 450000)
#ASSERT `What do I take as the partner` 2 1 TRUE 1000000 50000 500000 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What do I take as the partner` 1 0 FALSE 600000 0 500000 TRUE EQUALS JUST (`entitlement` TRUE 0 0 FALSE 0 600000)
#ASSERT `What do I take as the partner` 0 1 FALSE 600000 0 500000 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 70L(2), (3), 70ZG-70ZK -- what a relative takes`

-- Arguments: my place, lines further down, partners, child lines, issue not of a partner, parents, sibling lines, remote
-- sibling issue, grandparents, aunt and uncle lines, estate worth, chattels worth, statutory legacy.
-- Beside a partner (s 70L): the children's half of the balance is $225,000, between 2 child lines.
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a child, grandchild or remoter issue of the intestate` (LIST) 1 2 TRUE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 1000000 50000 500000 EQUALS JUST 112500
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a child, grandchild or remoter issue of the intestate` (LIST 3) 1 2 TRUE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 1000000 50000 500000 EQUALS JUST 37500
-- Where the partner takes the whole (s 70K), the children take nothing.
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a child, grandchild or remoter issue of the intestate` (LIST) 1 2 FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 1000000 50000 500000 EQUALS JUST 0
-- No partner (s 70ZG): $900,000 between 3 child lines; a grandchild in a family of 2; a great-grandchild three levels down.
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a child, grandchild or remoter issue of the intestate` (LIST) 0 3 FALSE 2 0 FALSE 0 0 900000 0 500000 EQUALS JUST 300000
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a child, grandchild or remoter issue of the intestate` (LIST 2) 0 3 FALSE 2 0 FALSE 0 0 900000 0 500000 EQUALS JUST 150000
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a child, grandchild or remoter issue of the intestate` (LIST 2, 2, 2) 0 2 FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 0 800000 0 500000 EQUALS JUST 50000
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a child, grandchild or remoter issue of the intestate` (LIST 0) 0 3 FALSE 2 0 FALSE 0 0 900000 0 500000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Parents (s 70ZH), and a parent where there are children.
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a parent of the intestate` (LIST) 0 0 FALSE 2 0 FALSE 0 0 900000 0 500000 EQUALS JUST 450000
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a parent of the intestate` (LIST) 0 1 FALSE 2 0 FALSE 0 0 900000 0 500000 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Siblings (s 70ZI): 3 lines; a nephew in a family of 2; a sibling's grandchild gets no share.
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a sibling of the intestate, or the child of a sibling who died` (LIST) 0 0 FALSE 0 3 FALSE 2 4 900000 0 500000 EQUALS JUST 300000
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a sibling of the intestate, or the child of a sibling who died` (LIST 2) 0 0 FALSE 0 3 FALSE 2 4 900000 0 500000 EQUALS JUST 150000
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a sibling of the intestate, or the child of a sibling who died` (LIST 2, 2) 0 0 FALSE 0 3 FALSE 2 4 900000 0 500000 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Grandparents (s 70ZJ); barred by a sibling's remoter issue (finding 2).
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a grandparent of the intestate` (LIST) 0 0 FALSE 0 0 FALSE 4 2 800000 0 500000 EQUALS JUST 200000
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `a grandparent of the intestate` (LIST) 0 0 FALSE 0 0 TRUE 4 2 800000 0 500000 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Aunts and uncles (s 70ZK): 4 lines; a cousin in a family of 4.
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `an aunt or uncle of the intestate, or the child (cousin) of an aunt or uncle who died` (LIST) 0 0 FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 4 800000 0 500000 EQUALS JUST 200000
#ASSERT `What do I take as a relative` `an aunt or uncle of the intestate, or the child (cousin) of an aunt or uncle who died` (LIST 4) 0 0 FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 4 800000 0 500000 EQUALS JUST 50000

§§ `s 3, s 70L(1)(b)(iii) -- interest on the statutory legacy`

-- $500,000 at 4.35% + 2% = 6.35% for 365 days is $31,750; for 73 days (1 January to 15 March 2026) a fifth of that.
#ASSERT `How much interest is added to my statutory legacy` 500000 4.35 (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 1 1 2027) EQUALS 31750
#ASSERT `How much interest is added to my statutory legacy` 500000 4.35 (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 15 3 2026) EQUALS 6350
#ASSERT `How much interest is added to my statutory legacy` 500000 4.35 (`d` 1 1 2026) (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS 0

§§ `s 70M -- the statutory legacy for a year`

#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest` 10 `of` 1005 EQUALS 1010
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest` 10 `of` 1004.9 EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest` 1 `of` 0.5 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `rounded to the nearest` 10 `of` (0 MINUS 4609.49) EQUALS (0 MINUS 4610)
-- Arguments: amount last calculated, index B, index C, amount in effect last year.
-- First year: A = $451,909; x 102/100 gives a variation of $9,038.18, rounded to $9,040: $460,949.
#ASSERT `What is the partner's statutory legacy for the year` 0 102 100 451909 EQUALS (`The statutory legacy for a year` WITH `the amount calculated` IS 460949, `the amount in effect` IS 460949)
-- A small variation ($460.949) is rounded to the dollar: $461.
#ASSERT `What is the partner's statutory legacy for the year` 460949 100.1 100 460949 EQUALS (`The statutory legacy for a year` WITH `the amount calculated` IS 461410, `the amount in effect` IS 461410)
-- A fall of 1%: -$4,609.49 rounds to -$4,610; $456,339 is calculated but does not take effect.
#ASSERT `What is the partner's statutory legacy for the year` 460949 99 100 460949 EQUALS (`The statutory legacy for a year` WITH `the amount calculated` IS 456339, `the amount in effect` IS 460949)
-- The next year runs from the reduced amount: +$9,126.78 rounds to $9,130: $465,469, in effect.
#ASSERT `What is the partner's statutory legacy for the year` 456339 102 100 460949 EQUALS (`The statutory legacy for a year` WITH `the amount calculated` IS 465469, `the amount in effect` IS 465469)
-- A last calculated amount below $451,909 is not A: A stays $451,909; +$225.95 rounds to $226.
#ASSERT `What is the partner's statutory legacy for the year` 440000 100.05 100 451909 EQUALS (`The statutory legacy for a year` WITH `the amount calculated` IS 452135, `the amount in effect` IS 452135)

§§ `Division 4 -- the partner's property election`

#ASSERT `Can I make a partner's property election` 1 2 TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I make a partner's property election` 1 2 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I make a partner's property election` 1 0 FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I make a partner's property election` 2 1 TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I make a partner's property election` 0 1 TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `By when must I be given the right to elect notice` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `the notice is due by` (`d` 31 3 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I be given the right to elect notice` FALSE (`d` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `the notice is due by` (`d` 14 1 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I be given the right to elect notice` TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `no notice is required, as I am the personal representative (s 70Q(3))`

#ASSERT `Was I given the right to elect notice in time` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 31 3 2027) (`d` 1 5 2027) EQUALS `done in time`
#ASSERT `Was I given the right to elect notice in time` (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 4 2027) (`d` 1 5 2027) EQUALS `not done in time`
#ASSERT `Was I given the right to elect notice in time` (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 31 3 2027) EQUALS `still open`
#ASSERT `Was I given the right to elect notice in time` (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 1 4 2027) EQUALS `not done in time`

-- Arguments: I am the administrator, day of the grant, notice given, date of the notice, Court extended, extended to.
#ASSERT `By when must I make my property election` TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the last day to elect is` (`d` 28 2 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I make my property election` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 20 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `the last day to elect is` (`d` 20 6 2027)
#ASSERT `By when must I make my property election` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `three months from the date of the right to elect notice, once it is given`
#ASSERT `By when must I make my property election` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 20 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 9 2027) EQUALS `the last day to elect is` (`d` 1 9 2027)

-- ... then election made, day of election, today.
#ASSERT `Is my property election in time` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 20 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 20 6 2027) (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST `done in time`
#ASSERT `Is my property election in time` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 20 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 21 6 2027) (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST `not done in time`
#ASSERT `Is my property election in time` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 20 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 20 6 2027) EQUALS JUST `still open`
#ASSERT `Is my property election in time` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 20 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 21 6 2027) EQUALS JUST `not done in time`
#ASSERT `Is my property election in time` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) (`d` 21 6 2027) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my property election in time` FALSE (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 20 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 9 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 9 2027) (`d` 1 10 2027) EQUALS JUST `done in time`
#ASSERT `Is my property election in time` TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 28 2 2027) (`d` 1 4 2027) EQUALS JUST `done in time`
#ASSERT `Is my property election in time` TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) TRUE (`d` 1 3 2027) (`d` 1 4 2027) EQUALS JUST `not done in time`

-- Arguments: price, my share, day of election, distribution day set, distribution day.
#ASSERT `What must I pay into the estate for the property` 600000 450000 (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `payment of` 150000 `by` (`d` 1 3 2028)
#ASSERT `What must I pay into the estate for the property` 600000 450000 (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 10 2027) EQUALS `payment of` 150000 `by` (`d` 30 9 2027)
#ASSERT `What must I pay into the estate for the property` 600000 450000 (`d` 1 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 6 2028) EQUALS `payment of` 150000 `by` (`d` 1 3 2028)
#ASSERT `What must I pay into the estate for the property` 400000 450000 (`d` 1 3 2027) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `payment of` 0 `by` (`d` 1 3 2028)
#ASSERT `What must I pay into the estate for the property` 600000 450000 (`d` 29 2 2028) FALSE (`d` 1 1 2000) EQUALS `payment of` 150000 `by` (`d` 28 2 2029)
